      "url": "https://x.com/nicgabunada/status/1984387803086799053",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/nicgabunada/status/1984387803086799053",
      "text": "🚨 Breaking: Michelin Guide just dropped its FIRST-EVER stars for the Philippines! 🇵🇭✨ Manila's culinary scene is leveling UP big time in the 2026 edition. One restaurant snagged TWO stars, eight more got one—proving Filipino flavors are world-class. Who's ready to splurge on these gems? \n\n**The Crown Jewel: TWO Michelin Stars**  \n• **Helm** (Makati) – Chef Josh Boutwood's intimate tasting menu? \"Deeply personal, precise, and profoundly expressive.\" Book NOW. \n\n**One Michelin Star Squad (all Metro Manila unless noted):**  \n• **Asador Alfonso** (Cavite) – Basque-inspired fire cooking magic.  \n• **Celera** (Manila) – Contemporary Asian fusion with PH twists.  \n• **Gallery by Chele** (BGC) – Farm-to-table excellence + a GREEN Star for sustainability! 🌿  \n• **Hapag** (Manila) – Modern Filipino soul food.  \n• **Kasa Palma** (Quezon City) – Spanish-Filipino vibes.  \n• **Linamnam** (Mandaluyong) – Innovative Pinoy heritage plates.  \n• **Toyo Eatery** (Mandaluyong) – Bold, boundary-pushing Filipino eats.  \n\nTotal: 108 spots honored, including 25 Bib Gourmands for affordable awesomeness. PH foodies, this is our moment—global eyes on us! What's your must-try first? Drop recs below. 🍴 #MichelinPH #ManilaEats #FilipinoCuisine #FoodieAlert",
